With End showing in the speed graph, each key has a yellow handle. How far a handle reaches sideways is the influence, which sets how long the ease lasts. Easy Ease gives both keys the same reach, which is why the move feels even. You want the move to start quickly and land softly. Drag the handle on the landing key at 1.2 s sideways along the bottom to make that ease longer. Then drag the handle on the start key at 0.2 s back toward its key to make that ease shorter.

Shape Bar's End that way and say done.

